              {
                "alt": "On the left side of the image, a table is shown with two columns. The left column is titled “1 divided by T ( K superscript negative 1 )” and \n                            the right column is titled “l n k”. The first row in the table has 0.00366 in the left column and 8.34 in the right column. The second row has \n                            0.00353 in the left column and 9.31 in the right column. The third row has 0.00341 on the left and 10.04 on the right. The fourth row has 0.00330 \n                            on the left and 10.90 on the right. The fifth row has 0.00320 on the left and 11.49 on the right. On the right side of the image, a graph is \n                            shown with the label “1 divided by T ( K superscript negative 1 )” on the x-axis and “l n k” on the y-axis. The horizontal axis has markings at \n                            0.0031, 0.0033, 0.0035 and 0.0037. The y-axis shows markings at intervals of 2 from 8 through 12. A decreasing linear trend line is drawn through \n                            five points at the coordinates: (0.00366, 8.34), (0.00353, 9.31), (0.00341, 10.04), (0.00330, 10.90), and (0.00320,11.49). An equation is shown on \n                            the graph. It shows the formula “y equals negative 6870 times x plus 33.5.”.",
